--------------------------------------------------------------------
EXTRACTION RESULT (Magic ext2spice, all blocks)
--------------------------------------------------------------------
Block              | Extracted FET devices | Reason
-------------------|----------------------|--------------------------
cp_pmos_array      | 0                    | Poly touches diff, no overlap
cp_nmos_array      | 0                    | Poly touches diff, no overlap
vco_stage_unit     | 0                    | Poly touches diff, no overlap
sky130_vco_layout  | 0                    | Poly touches diff, no overlap
sky130_bias_layout | 0                    | Poly touches diff, no overlap

ROOT CAUSE: Magic's sky130A extractor requires poly to OVERLAP (cross
through) diffusion to form a FET device. The scripted layout generator
placed poly ADJACENT to (touching at the boundary of) diffusion, not
overlapping it. Magic reads nodes (ndif, pdif, poly) but never generates
a 'fet' line in the .ext file for any cell.

EVIDENCE:
  cp_nmos_array.ext: 0 'fet' lines (nodes: ndif, poly, li only)
  vco_stage_unit.ext: 0 'fet' lines (nodes: ndif, pdif, poly, nw)
  sky130_vco_layout.ext: 0 'fet' lines
  sky130_bias_layout.ext: 0 'fet' lines
  cp_pmos_array.ext: 0 'fet' lines (nodes: pdif, poly, li, nw)

Specific geometry (Magic internal units, 1 unit = 0.005 um = 5 nm):
  cp_nmos_array: ndiff rect {2,2,4,5}, poly rect {4,1,8,6}
    -> poly left-edge x=4 == ndiff right-edge x=4: TOUCH only, 0 nm overlap
  vco_stage_unit: ndiff {3,6,7,10}, poly {3,10,7,11}
    -> poly bottom y=10 == ndiff top y=10: TOUCH only, 0 nm overlap
  cp_pmos_array: pdiff {4,4,6,12}, poly {6,2,10,14}
    -> poly left x=6 == pdiff right x=6: TOUCH only, 0 nm overlap

