--------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT THIS MEANS FOR SIGN-OFF
--------------------------------------------------------------------
The layout cells contain the correct layer types (pdiff, ndiff, poly,
locali, metal1, metal2, nwell, via1) and the device dimensions match
the schematic (e.g. PMOS W=4u/L=2u => 12 pdiff fingers at the correct
pitch). The DRC violations also confirm real geometry exists.

However, to achieve device extraction, the scripted layout must be
corrected so that poly overlaps diff (not just touches). In sky130
the minimum poly enclosure of diff is 0.13 um; the poly must extend
past the diff edge (actacting as gate oxide) with source and drain
regions on each side.

FIX REQUIRED (route_to: custom-layout):
  Move poly rectangles to overlap diff by >= 0.13 um (26 magic units
  at the 1 unit = 5 nm scale) on each side. Specifically:
  - cp_pmos_array: pdiff at {4..6, 4..12}; poly must start at x < 4
    (e.g. poly {3,2,7,14} gives 2-unit overlap each side)
  - cp_nmos_array: ndiff {2..4, 2..5}; poly must overlap (e.g. {3,1,5,6})
  - vco_stage_unit: similarly shift poly to cross diff vertically
  This will also resolve many of the DRC violations (poly.4 poly-to-diff
  spacing errors fire because they are touching, not properly crossing).

